{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: amendment 4 lanes L/B at 04797d8c6eb5d9792d4c2e0b93a4d7896a5f7c67, all 22 artifacts with notes/amendment4-log.md first. The implementation covers the stated sizes and migration/CAS cases and passes the baseline gates. One P2 numeric-width limit conflicts with unlimited logical entries and the EntryLine byte contract.\n\nP2: Preserve logical line lengths above 2^32-1 before chunking. plan collects safe-integer line byte lengths in lens, then close passes Uint32Array.from(lens) to segment. That wraps a 4 GiB line to 0, or 4 GiB plus one to 1. segment compares the unchanged EntryLine.bytes with that wrapped value and refuses it as invalid-input, alleging that the source changed. The line never reaches entryFile/chunking. Body, batchSize and batch use the same UInt32 representation.\n\nAn independent three-case metadata-width control calls the actual commitFor with a normal genesis and an EntryLine reporting 2^32-1, 2^32 or 2^32+1 bytes. A signed checkpoint and fixed canonical tail pass the metadata boundary. The first case reaches the large-body hashing stage, where the control deliberately stops; the other cases fail beforehand with 'entry 1 was 0/1 bytes and is now 4294967296/7'. Assertions for all three pass. This is a representation/control-flow proof: no 4 GiB object was allocated or hashed, and it is not a claim to have published or verified a fully signed 4 GiB entry. Every real unchanged source of those lengths meets the same wrapped comparison before its body is consumed.\n\nUse a numeric representation that preserves the accepted safe-integer length range across measurement, placement, hashing and staging. Add boundary controls without allocating a multi-gigabyte body, plus ordinary actual chunk publication coverage. Retain validation that a source genuinely changing length is refused. Do not add a logical-entry cap or weaken the complete-content requirement to fit the storage representation.\n\nArchitecture: layout.ts supplies deterministic byte/count placement, ChunkedLine lengths/digests, chunk sizing and multi-level fan-out shared with the index reader/verifier. Files are planned into bounded chunks, closed segments and unchanged trees are reused by ID, and both commitFor and publish guard planned objects before remote effects. A first layout-2 checkpoint follows the confirmed parent's through+1, not a still-pending cohort, and later checkpoints preserve from. The oversized already-sealed unpublished entry is chunked; historical layout-1 segments are retained and verify unchanged. Correcting lens width completes the new part-reader boundary without altering these rules.\n\nLate publication remains a caller/Room responsibility, accurately stated in the report. L reads back after a refused push, confirms its exact commit if observed, stops at the parent with refused, or returns unexpected-writer with current. open can build on a caller-identified late own commit. The tests exercise both CAS orders for C and D, including the layout switch. Lane B maps known pre-update Artifacts codes and rejected status to refused; landed status, unknown codes and ambiguous failures stay distinct. A later refusal, expiry, absence or read of the parent does not prove an earlier unknown push cannot apply. The Room's durable outstanding-commit list and retry policy are explicitly still due in a separate request.\n\nSecurity: The verifier reassembles chunks, checks their shape, length, digest and entry seq, then applies the existing hash/signature/authority/policy replay checks. It checks layout transitions, exact segment starts, closed segments, byte limits, retained digest paths and shard placement, with named failures. The strict decoder distinguishes canonical ChunkedLine from entries and rejects extra layout/stub fields. Push refusal detail remains token-redacted. The Artifacts code allowlist is narrow and gives precedence to a ref's actual status. Unknown codes require evidence before being treated as definite. No live deployment or credential work was performed by checker.\n\nSimplification: Shared Placement, chunk and fan-out rules reduce independent interpretations between writer, index and verifier. The additive EntryLine/RetainedRef.read interfaces preserve layout-1 callers while permitting large content in parts. Keep the same simple contract for byte lengths throughout; a typed-array storage shortcut must not silently narrow it. The public readLogFiles/readPublishedEntries and verifier still assemble full logical files/log views; the bounded publishing path is distinct from those whole-value APIs, and future Room chunk storage and large-entry delivery remain explicit work.\n\nValidation: Fresh detached checkout; npm ci 374 packages. All workspace type checks passed. Clean root suite passed 1,719 tests with one skipped, including log 185 Node/180 workerd and Git 164 Node. Separate Git Workers 8 and Git log Workers 12 passed; the latter exercises a real local git pre-receive refusal and one push. The three independent metadata-width assertions passed in a separate custom include outside the baseline test glob, and the scratch file was removed. The first probe supplied only 447 tail bytes for a requested 512; this was a checker fixture error corrected before the successful run. No implementation source was changed, and the checkout is clean. Logs: /tmp/artroom-checker-log-Am4-LB-v1-{ci,types,tests,git-workers,git-log}.log. Probe source/results: /tmp/artroom-checker-log-Am4-LB-v1-diagnostics.\n\nEvidence/coverage: All 22 changed artifact paths exactly match the diff against main 9bb700b6; each changed file/diff was read, including the full 291-line primary report, 1,084-line publisher, layout/tree modules and both new acceptance suites. The remaining 529 exact tree paths are credited to reviewed main; no deletion. The 5,000,000-entry case preserves the full count but uses one-byte synthetic middle lines, and does not verify their signatures. The 5,000 shared-prefix retained contexts, 20 MiB policy/context, 200,000-recipient notification, 100,000-path revert, 2,000-checker activation and 500 recomputations run as documented. Refusal size is scaled from Artifacts' 32 MiB to B in MemoryGit. The 38 mutation kills are builder-reported, not independently repeated. No new deployed layout-2 proof is claimed.\n\nIntegration/full scope: Founding has landed at main 1f4f1f0b; its 553-file tree is exactly the approved f493953a candidate, independently confirmed with no differences. Preserve that work when merging this branch. This review covers only f77571a6's L/B delivery. Room layout-2 adoption, durable unknown identities and admin attention, large-entry storage/API/subscribe delivery, coordinated live acceptance through the deployed sandbox, MCP cleanup, Am3 deadline recovery and full pi runtime remain on their own requests. None is removed by schedule estimates.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3f6c3f3dd79c782fa2af7f4a4ed0c371c3cc0351","binding":"assigned","head":"04797d8c6eb5d9792d4c2e0b93a4d7896a5f7c67","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:835cb587377aa1b5f5594a4587e4e7a2023a567f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6f64ec60259345625566faa53cdd1962507e1049\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b88518016f38f1495c4b1cf78e23608487d73cdd","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}